        },
        {
          "label_path": [
            "b"
          ],
          "prompt_markdown": "Hence determine the coefficient of $x^2$ in the expansion of $\\left(x^2 + 5\\right)\\left(2x - \\frac{3}{x}\\right)^4$.",
          "marks": 2,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            4
          ]
        }
      ],
      "mark_scheme_items": [
        {
          "sequence_number": 1,
          "mark_code": "B1",
          "content_markdown": "$\\left(2x\\right)^4$ and $\\left(\\frac{\\pm 3}{x}\\right)^4$",
          "guidance_markdown": "May be seen in a full expansion. This can be implied by $16x^4$ and $+\\frac{81}{x^4}$ unless they are clearly using $+\\frac{3}{x}$ throughout.",
          "is_final_answer": false,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 2,
          "mark_code": "B1",
          "content_markdown": "$4(2x)^3\\left(\\frac{-3}{x}\\right)+6(2x)^2\\left(\\frac{-3}{x}\\right)^2+4(2x)\\left(\\frac{-3}{x}\\right)^3$",
          "guidance_markdown": "Correct combination of numerical coefficients for the middle three terms. Can be implied by a correct full expansion.",
          "is_final_answer": false,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 3,
          "mark_code": "M1",
          "content_markdown": "$\\left[16x^4\\right]+k_1x^2+k_2\\left[x^0\\right]+k_3x^{-2}\\left[+81x^{-4}\\right]$",
          "guidance_markdown": "OE Powers now simplified correctly with *their* $k_1, k_2, k_3 \\neq 0$.",
          "is_final_answer": false,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 4,
          "mark_code": "A1",
          "content_markdown": "$16x^4-96x^2+216-216x^{-2}+81x^{-4}$",
          "guidance_markdown": "OE",
          "is_final_answer": true,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
          "source_page_numbers": [
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_number": 5,
          "mark_code": "M1",
          "content_markdown": "Use of (their 216) + 5×(their -96) only, to arrive at the coefficient of $x^2$",
          "guidance_markdown": "Other terms may be seen.",
          "is_final_answer": false,
          "is_alternative_method": false,
